  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["J7", "J8"],
      "pins": ["J7.1", "J7.2", "J7.3", "J7.4", "J8.1", "J8.2", "J8.3", "J8.4"],
      "nets": ["+12V", "FAN_0_TACH", "FAN_1_TACH", "GND"],
      "observed": "On the Power sheet the two 4-pin fan headers are wired as: J7/J8 pin 1 = +12V, pin 2 = FAN_0_TACH / FAN_1_TACH, pin 3 = an unconnected auto-net (local label 'Conn_01x04_Pin'), pin 4 = no-connect. No pin of J7/J8 is tied to GND, and the +12V supply sits on pin 1 rather than pin 2.",
      "expected": "The specification states the fan supply is on pin 2 ('the two fan-header 12 V pins (J7/J8 pin 2)'), and the tach inputs are described as TVS-clamped to GND, which requires a ground return on the header. The intended header must carry +12V on pin 2, a GND pin, and the tach signal on the remaining pin.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Also on this net: ... the two fan-header 12 V pins (J7/J8 pin 2)."},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "power.kicad_sch (Power sheet, right side): J7 pin1 -> +12V, pin2 -> FAN_0_TACH, pin3 -> Conn_01x04_Pin, pin4 -> X; J8 pin1 -> +12V, pin2 -> FAN_1_TACH, pin3 -> Conn_01x04_Pin, pin4 -> X; no GND symbol on either header."}
      ],
      "impact": "A fan cabled for the intended pinout (12 V on pin 2, GND on pin 1) would have its ground wire driven by the board's +12 V rail and its supply wire fed the tach signal: the 12 V rail is shorted to the fan's ground through the connector, the fans do not spin, the tach lines are not referenced to the fan's own ground, and the firmware's fan-stall fault (NUM_FANS = 2) would trip, aborting any run.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The power, thermocouple, MCU and heater paths match the specification, but the two fan headers J7/J8 are mis-wired relative to the intended design: +12 V is placed on pin 1 and the tach signal on pin 2 (the spec puts 12 V on pin 2), and no header pin is connected to GND, leaving the fans without a return path."
}

